            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allyson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "#AllrecipesAllstarsCanada.\n#Facelessnomore\n\nI love a good chowder and this was very tasty. I am not a fan of canned soup, so I omitted that, and used a cup of cream mixed with a TBSP cornstarch. I added less milk than was called for, as I do like it thicker than most.\n\nI served with https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/7146/cheddar-bay-biscuits/\nThose are a big hit in my family as it reminds us of the biscuits at red lobster.",
            "datePublished": "2018-03-23T20:09:58.470Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amber Petit"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had this very chowder in Ireland and did a search in hopes of finding one similar and was THIRILLED to see that Durty Nelly has posted and shared his recipe. I did not have shrimp so made mine with salmon and mahi mahi. I also added a bunch of chopped parsley since I had it on hand. The family loved it!!! Excellent chowder!!",
            "datePublished": "2018-02-16T14:43:01.887Z"
          }
